  ('mth-121-calculus', 'MTH 121: Functions, Limits, Differentiation & Integration', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences', 'Mathematics', '100 Level', '$\textrm{Use}$ $\textrm{L''Hopital''s}$ $\textrm{Rule}$ $\textrm{to}$ $\textrm{evaluate}$ $\lim_{x \to 0} [\sin(x)/x]$$\textrm{.}$', '["$1$", "$\\textrm{does}$ $\\textrm{not}$ $\\textrm{exist}$", "$\\infty$", "$0$"]'::jsonb, 0, '$\textrm{This}$ $\textrm{is}$ $\textrm{a}$ $0/0$ $\textrm{form.}$ $\textrm{Differentiate}$ $\textrm{numerator}$ $\textrm{and}$ $\textrm{denominator}$ $\textrm{separately:}$ $\dfrac{d}{dx}[\sin{\left(x \right)}]$ $=$ $\cos{\left(x \right)}$ $\textrm{and}$ $\dfrac{d}{dx}[x] = 1$$\textrm{.}$ $\textrm{By}$ $\textrm{L''Hopital''s}$ $\textrm{Rule,}$ $\lim_{x \to 0} \frac{\sin{\left(x \right)}}{x}$ $=$ $\lim_{x \to 0} \dfrac{\cos{\left(x \right)}}{1}$ $=$ $\cos{\left(0 \right)}$ $=$ $1$$\textrm{.}$', 'Indeterminate Forms and L''Hopital''s Rule', false),
